{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_gossip", "label": "Gossip replication", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Local writes are immediate; gossip is only for propagation, so writes converge eventually \u2014 usually within 1-2 rounds."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_gossipinterval", "label": "gossipInterval", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Default 1s balances propagation speed against gossip-bandwidth cost; lower means faster convergence and more chatter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_max_gossip_bytes", "label": "max-gossip-bytes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defaults to 1 MiB and is clamped to remote.max-frame-bytes. Without it a large store produced one frame past the wire cap, rejected on its 4-byte length prefix; the transport answered by dropping the connection carrying heartbeats, membership gossip and every cross-node tell \u2014 so the store did not converge at all while killing one peer link per tick."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_remote_max_frame_bytes", "label": "remote.max-frame-bytes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_full_state_slicing", "label": "Full state sliced to fit one frame", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No delta tracking and no per-peer receipt history, so gossip volume is proportional to total state size, not update rate. Slicing is safe because merging is per key and an absent key means no information, not deletion."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_crdt_merge", "label": "Per-key CRDT merge (idempotent, commutative)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_subscribe", "label": "dd.subscribe(key, listener)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fires synchronously after every merge that changes the local value (deep-equal via the CRDT toJSON); idempotent updates do not fire, and a subscription is local \u2014 it sees the local value, not the cluster true value."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_random_peer_selection", "label": "Random-peer-per-tick selection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Round-robin would be more predictable but creates synchronized waves; random-peer disperses load and converges in O(log N) rounds, helped further by multi-hop re-gossip."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_tombstones", "label": "CRDT tombstones are never garbage collected", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept permanently so a stale gossip cannot resurrect a removed key; over a long-lived store with heavy churn, tombstone accumulation is the practical cost."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_member_removed_noop", "label": "MemberRemoved is a no-op for DistributedData", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is no per-peer state to clean up \u2014 no version vector, no receipt history \u2014 so a departed node simply stops being a gossip target and a rejoining replica needs no special handling."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_skipped_keys_metric", "label": "distributed_data_gossip_skipped_keys_total", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single key whose encoding exceeds the budget cannot be sliced further, is skipped, and does not converge \u2014 the replica warns rate-limited and increments this counter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_anti_entropy_scaling", "label": "Anti-entropy gossip scaling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_partition_no_bridge", "label": "Gossip does not bridge partitions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "By design \u2014 CRDTs guarantee eventual convergence, not real-time delivery, so partition-tolerant read flows must work with stale data."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_gossip", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_gossipinterval", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_gossip", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_full_state_slicing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_full_state_slicing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_max_gossip_bytes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_max_gossip_bytes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_remote_max_frame_bytes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_max_gossip_bytes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_skipped_keys_metric", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_full_state_slicing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_crdt_merge", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_crdt_merge", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_subscribe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_crdt_merge", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_tombstones", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_gossip", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_random_peer_selection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_random_peer_selection", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_member_removed_noop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/distributed-data/replication.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_gossip", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_distributed_data_replication_anti_entropy_scaling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.